"talquetamab":{rl:"Given SC with step-up doses to 0.4 mg/kg weekly or 0.8 mg/kg every 2 weeks per label; 48-hour hospitalization after step-up doses; REMS drug with boxed CRS and ICANS.",rh:"Fever, hypotension, hypoxia, confusion, inability to eat or swallow, rapid weight loss or severe rash typically prompt holding the next dose and notifying the provider.",ml:"GPRC5D x CD3 bispecific IgG4 antibody; labeled (accelerated) for relapsed or refractory multiple myeloma after at least four prior lines.",mp:"GPRC5D is expressed in keratinized tissue, explaining dysgeusia, nail and skin toxicity; it remains active after BCMA-directed therapy."},
"elranatamab":{rl:"Given SC with fixed step-up doses of 12 and 32 mg, then 76 mg weekly per label; hospitalization after step-up doses; REMS drug with boxed CRS and ICANS.",rh:"Fever, hypotension, hypoxia, confusion, tremor, aphasia or signs of infection typically prompt holding the next dose and notifying the provider.",ml:"BCMA x CD3 bispecific IgG2 antibody; labeled (accelerated) for relapsed or refractory multiple myeloma after at least four prior lines.",mp:"Fixed-dose BCMA bispecific with interval extension to every 2 and then every 4 weeks in responders; CRS, ICANS and infections dominate toxicity."},
"linvoseltamab":{rl:"Given IV with step-up doses of 5 and 25 mg, then 200 mg per label; 24-hour hospitalization after step-up doses; REMS drug with boxed CRS and ICANS.",rh:"Fever, hypotension, hypoxia, confusion, tremor, aphasia or signs of infection typically prompt holding the next dose and notifying the provider.",ml:"BCMA x CD3 bispecific IgG4 antibody given IV; labeled (accelerated) for relapsed or refractory multiple myeloma after at least four prior lines.",mp:"The only IV BCMA bispecific; step-up infusions run over 4 hours, and VGPR or better allows every-4-week dosing."},
"epcoritamab":{rl:"Given SC in 28-day cycles with step-up doses of 0.16 and 0.8 mg (plus 3 mg in FL), then 48 mg per label; boxed CRS and ICANS, with 24-hour hospitalization after the first full dose in DLBCL.",rh:"Fever, hypotension, hypoxia, confusion, aphasia, signs of infection or tumor lysis labs typically prompt holding the next dose and notifying the provider.",ml:"CD20 x CD3 bispecific IgG1 antibody; labeled for relapsed or refractory DLBCL, high-grade B-cell lymphoma and follicular lymphoma, including with lenalidomide and rituximab.",mp:"CD20 x CD3 bispecifics (epcoritamab, glofitamab, mosunetuzumab) cause CRS mainly after the first full dose; step-up dosing and corticosteroid premedication reduce severity."}
