"trastuzumab-deruxtecan":{rl:"HER2-directed ADC given at 5.4 mg/kg IV every 3 weeks (6.4 mg/kg for gastric cancer) per label, diluted in dextrose 5% only; highly emetogenic, with antiemetic premedication typical.",rh:"New cough, dyspnea, fever or hypoxia (possible ILD/pneumonitis), neutropenia, LVEF decline and severe vomiting typically prompt holding and provider notification.",ml:"Trastuzumab linked to the topoisomerase I inhibitor DXd; labeled for HER2-positive, HER2-low and HER2-ultralow breast cancer, HER2-mutant NSCLC, HER2-positive gastric cancer and HER2-positive (IHC 3+) solid tumors.",mp:"Boxed warning for ILD/pneumonitis and embryo-fetal toxicity; its bystander effect made HER2-low breast cancer a treatable category (DESTINY-Breast04)."},
