"datopotamab-deruxtecan":{rl:"Trop-2-directed ADC given at 6 mg/kg IV (up to 540 mg for patients 90 kg or more) every 3 weeks per label, diluted in dextrose 5% with a 0.2-micron filter; steroid mouthwash and lubricant eye drops are part of care.",rh:"New cough, dyspnea or fever, eye pain or vision changes, and severe stomatitis limiting intake typically prompt holding and provider notification.",ml:"Anti-Trop-2 antibody linked to the topoisomerase I inhibitor DXd; labeled for pretreated HR-positive, HER2-negative and triple-negative breast cancer and for EGFR-mutated NSCLC (accelerated approval).",mp:"Same deruxtecan payload as Enhertu but aimed at Trop-2, with stomatitis, ocular surface toxicity and ILD as the key toxicities."},
"enfortumab-vedotin":{rl:"Nectin-4-directed ADC given at 1.25 mg/kg IV over 30 minutes (up to 125 mg) per label, Days 1, 8 and 15 of 28 alone or Days 1 and 8 of 21 with pembrolizumab; glucose and skin are reviewed before each dose.",rh:"Rash, blistering or mucosal lesions, blood glucose above 250 mg/dL, worsening neuropathy, cough or dyspnea, and eye symptoms typically prompt holding and provider notification.",ml:"Anti-Nectin-4 antibody linked to MMAE (microtubule inhibitor); labeled for urothelial cancer, including with pembrolizumab for advanced disease and around cystectomy for muscle-invasive bladder cancer.",mp:"Boxed warning for SJS/TEN; hyperglycemia and DKA occur even without diabetes, and EV plus pembrolizumab (EV-302) improved survival over platinum chemotherapy."},
"tisotumab-vedotin":{rl:"Tissue factor-directed ADC given at 2 mg/kg IV over 30 minutes (up to 200 mg) every 3 weeks per label, with steroid and vasoconstrictor eye drops before, cooling eye pads during, and lubricating drops throughout.",rh:"Eye pain, redness or vision change, significant bleeding including epistaxis, worsening neuropathy and new cough or dyspnea typically prompt holding and provider notification.",ml:"Anti-tissue factor antibody linked to MMAE; labeled for recurrent or metastatic cervical cancer progressing on or after chemotherapy.",mp:"Boxed warning for ocular toxicity; epistaxis is common because the antibody targets tissue factor."},
"mirvetuximab-soravtansine":{rl:"FRα-directed ADC given at 6 mg/kg adjusted ideal body weight IV every 3 weeks per label, starting at 1 mg/min, diluted in dextrose 5% with a PES filter; eye exams and eye drops are part of care.",rh:"Blurred vision, eye pain or photophobia, new cough or dyspnea, and worsening neuropathy typically prompt holding and provider notification.",ml:"Anti-folate receptor alpha antibody linked to the maytansinoid DM4; labeled for FRα-positive, platinum-resistant ovarian, fallopian tube or primary peritoneal cancer after 1 to 3 prior regimens.",mp:"Boxed warning for ocular toxicity (keratopathy, blurred vision); dosed on adjusted ideal body weight and requires an FDA-approved FRα test."},
"brentuximab-vedotin":{rl:"CD30-directed ADC given as a 30-minute IV infusion, 1.2 mg/kg (up to 120 mg) every 2 weeks with AVD or 1.8 mg/kg (up to 180 mg) every 3 weeks as monotherapy per label; neuropathy and CBC are reviewed before each dose.",rh:"New confusion, memory loss, weakness or vision change (possible PML), worsening neuropathy, fever with neutropenia, severe abdominal pain and blistering rash typically prompt holding and provider notification.",ml:"Anti-CD30 antibody linked to MMAE; labeled for classical Hodgkin lymphoma (adult and pediatric previously untreated, consolidation, relapsed), sALCL, CD30-expressing PTCL, pcALCL, mycosis fungoides and relapsed large B-cell lymphoma.",mp:"Boxed warning for PML from JC virus; contraindicated with bleomycin because of pulmonary toxicity, which is why ECHELON-1 used A+AVD."}
