"gemtuzumab-ozogamicin":{rl:"Given IV over 2 hours, 3 mg/m2 (up to one 4.5 mg vial) on Days 1, 4 and 7 with daunorubicin and cytarabine per label, with premedication; boxed warning for hepatic VOD/SOS.",rh:"Infusion reactions, right upper quadrant pain, rapid weight gain, ascites, rising bilirubin or bleeding typically prompt interrupting the infusion or holding the dose and notifying the provider.",ml:"CD33-directed calicheamicin antibody-drug conjugate; labeled for newly diagnosed and relapsed or refractory CD33-positive AML.",mp:"First ADC approved (2000), withdrawn in 2010 and reapproved in 2017 with a lower fractionated dose; hepatic VOD/SOS is the boxed toxicity."},
"belantamab-mafodotin":{rl:"Given IV over about 30 minutes at 2.5 mg/kg every 3 weeks with bortezomib and dexamethasone for 8 cycles, then alone, per label; eye exams precede each dose.",rh:"Blurred vision, decreased visual acuity, eye pain or dryness, corneal findings on exam or low platelets typically prompt holding the dose and notifying the provider.",ml:"BCMA-directed antibody-drug conjugate carrying MMAF; labeled for relapsed or refractory multiple myeloma after at least two prior lines including a proteasome inhibitor and an immunomodulatory agent.",mp:"The MMAF payload causes corneal epithelial keratopathy (boxed warning); afucosylation of the antibody enhances ADCC."},
"telisotuzumab-vedotin":{rl:"Given IV over 30 minutes at 1.9 mg/kg (maximum 190 mg) every 2 weeks per label; peripheral neuropathy, pneumonitis and ocular surface toxicity are key risks.",rh:"New cough, dyspnea or hypoxia, worsening neuropathy, eye pain or visual changes, or infusion reactions typically prompt holding the dose and notifying the provider.",ml:"c-Met-directed antibody-drug conjugate carrying MMAE; labeled for previously treated nonsquamous NSCLC with high c-Met protein overexpression (accelerated approval).",mp:"Patient selection is by c-Met protein IHC, which differs from MET exon 14 skipping mutations targeted by capmatinib and tepotinib."},
"tagraxofusp":{rl:"Given IV over 15 minutes at 12 mcg/kg daily on Days 1 to 5 of a 21-day cycle per label with premedication; the first cycle is typically inpatient; boxed warning for capillary leak.",rh:"Albumin decline, rapid weight gain, new edema, hypotension, dyspnea or rising transaminases typically prompt holding the dose and notifying the provider.",ml:"CD123-directed IL-3 and truncated diphtheria toxin fusion protein; labeled for blastic plasmacytoid dendritic cell neoplasm in adults and children 2 years and older.",mp:"The diphtheria toxin fragment ADP-ribosylates elongation factor 2 to halt protein synthesis; capillary leak syndrome is the boxed warning."},
"denileukin-diftitox":{rl:"Given IV over 60 minutes at 9 mcg/kg/day on Days 1 through 5 of a 21-day cycle per label, with premedication in early cycles; boxed warning for capillary leak.",rh:"Low albumin, rapid weight gain, edema, hypotension, infusion reactions, visual changes or rising transaminases typically prompt holding the dose and notifying the provider.",ml:"IL-2 and diphtheria toxin fusion protein targeting CD25; labeled for relapsed or refractory stage I-III cutaneous T-cell lymphoma after at least one prior systemic therapy.",mp:"Diphtheria toxin inhibits EF-2 by ADP-ribosylation; the reformulated product (Lymphir) replaced Ontak, which was discontinued in 2014."}
